        "original_id": "40be59c5-87a8-5204-8488-7fae04a26f78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah National Park, Virginia, Rappahannock County, Culpeper County, Chesapeake Bay\n- Rivers: Hazel River, Covington River, Rappahannock River\n- Protected Areas: Shenandoah National Park\n- Concepts: River systems, tributaries\n\nFacts:\n- Shenandoah National Park is a national park in Virginia that encompasses part of the Blue Ridge Mountains.\n- The Hazel River rises in Shenandoah National Park and flows generally eastward through Rappahannock County and Culpeper County.\n- The Covington River system flows via the Hazel River to the Rappahannock River.\n- The Rappahannock River is a tributary of Chesapeake Bay.",
